  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "5:1-3 is not glossed (As-Sa'di gives two readings of «وإن تعجب»). Their claim (5:4-11) is framed «بزعمهم»; the chains and the Fire (5:16-25) are never drawn or glossed. 6-7 address the Prophet ﷺ: no plate on him. Light for «وإن ربك لذو مغفرة للناس على ظلمهم» (it leaves before «لشديد العقاب»), a lamp for «ولكل قوم هاد». Their demand (7:1-9) is framed as an excuse. STAGING v4: c1 (5): the deniers of the resurrection, three faceless men in dark robes in a town by day (no women, at most three for a blamed group). 5:1-3 addresses the Prophet ﷺ: wide, nobody faces an empty side. They shake their heads at their claim (5:5, 5:9: When we are dust...), framed by As-Sa'di's gloss (impossible in their claim); no speech arcs (their addressee is not drawn). The camera holds on them for those who disbelieved in their Lord and through the shackles and the Fire (5:16-25): nothing of the Hereafter is drawn, no plate, nobody leaves or fades. c2 (6) stays ambient: they hasten the Prophet ﷺ for the punishment (their behaviour toward him), then His forgiveness and severe punishment: quiet over 6:1-4 and 6:10-20; the plate for your Lord is the possessor of forgiveness is now geometric (a light plate must not start on His attribute). c3 (7) stays ambient: their demand for a sign sent down to him and Allah's words to him (quiet over 7:10-12); a light plate for every people has a guide. The cover now shows the deniers shaking their heads (5:5)."
